# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — this repo's guard-kit consumer knob file; set what this repo overrides beyond the kit defaults, and the policy rosters it binds

# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §check-door-binding — this repo's own surfaces beyond the kit roots that assertion C sweeps: the root README and the served docs tree, each entry a whole tree rather than a page roster so a page added later is swept unedited
GUARD_KIT_DOOR_ROOTS[] = README.md
GUARD_KIT_DOOR_ROOTS[] = docs

# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §compare-settings-allow — witnesses that a local-overlay glob is too broad; probes, not a roster, so no completeness is claimed
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git reset --hard)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git clean -fd)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git push --force)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git rm -r src)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git checkout -- TASK-QUEUE.md)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git stash clear)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(gh repo delete owner/repo --yes)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(gh api -X DELETE /repos/owner/repo)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(gh release delete v0.24.0 --yes)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(gh secret delete TOKEN)
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_PROBES[] = Bash(git worktree remove --force .)

# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §compare-settings-allow — breadth ruled intended; exact-string keyed, so re-spelling or narrowing the glob returns it to the narrowing candidates. The reasons are this project's own operator rulings, consumer values a kit never carries
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_DECLARED[Bash(git worktree *)] = worktree isolation is mandated rather than optional here — agent-dispatch-guard refuses a read-only-type dispatch that does not carry it — and the harness creates those trees and best-effort auto-cleans them, so the force-removal this breadth reaches destroys only disposable child state — and the iteration boundary now refuses on residue the auto-clean missed (lifecycle-kit/SPEC.md §bin/enter-stage.sh), which makes the reap a required session act rather than an optional one
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_DECLARED[Bash(gh api *)] = operator-ruled 2026-08-23 out of guard-grant-review, whose review walked all 105 committed Bash( entries and found nothing to narrow among the four gh globs. The ops surface this serves is repo-settings desired state, which is read and reconciled through arbitrary api paths and methods, so no glob narrower than the binary bounds it — a Bash rule's * spans / and .. by the vendor's own matcher semantics, which is why the narrowing question is a breadth ruling rather than a glob-authoring one
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_DECLARED[Bash(gh repo *)] = operator-ruled 2026-08-23 out of guard-grant-review, on the same review. The destructive form this reaches is gh repo delete, guarded host-side by the delete_repo scope a stock gh login does not carry, so the breadth reaches a command the credential must separately be entitled to run
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_DECLARED[Bash(gh release *)] = operator-ruled 2026-08-23 out of guard-grant-review, on the same review. This is the sharpest of the four — gh release delete destroys one of this project's two shipping transports — and it is declared rather than narrowed because the close stage cuts, edits and verifies releases itself (RELEASING.md steps 4-6) across subcommands no fixed glob enumerates
GUARD_KIT_BREADTH_DECLARED[Bash(gh secret *)] = operator-ruled 2026-08-23 out of guard-grant-review, on the same review. Secret rotation is the ops workflow it serves, and a rotation is a set-then-verify pair whose argument shape is the secret name, which is exactly what a glob cannot bound

# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §Consumer rules — this repo's own rules, a command the shell guard runs ahead of its generic ruleset
GUARD_KIT_CONSUMER_RULES_CMD[] = bash
GUARD_KIT_CONSUMER_RULES_CMD[] = scripts/guard-rules.sh

# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — this harness build carries no dedicated Glob or Grep tool in either session class, probed with a ToolSearch selecting both in a main and in a dispatched session, so guard-kit rules `find_glob` and `git_grep` stay inert and bare find and grep stay the working forms
GUARD_KIT_SEARCH_TOOLS =

# spec: guard-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — the policy rosters this repo relies on, bound at the members its guard decides with so a kit default's move moves no decision here (Policy-as-choice); each read-only member keeps its form declaration from the kit's table
GUARD_KIT_RO_BINS[] = grep
GUARD_KIT_RO_BINS[] = egrep
GUARD_KIT_RO_BINS[] = fgrep
GUARD_KIT_RO_BINS[] = rg
GUARD_KIT_RO_BINS[] = head
GUARD_KIT_RO_BINS[] = tail
